# P41: drive the pickers drawn in SwiftCrossUI views -- the wheel, the rows -- and AppKit's own clock.
#
# queue item 31 left "the Swift clock, rows and wheel are not driven by an action file". On AppKit
# the wheel (_SwiftWheelDatePicker) and the rows (_SwiftRowsDatePicker) are SwiftCrossUI views and the
# clock is NSDatePicker's own (nativeTimePresentation = .clock). GTK draws the other way round for the
# clock and rows; P41-swift-wheel-rows-clock-gtk4.actions drives that one.
#
# Judged by the binding, not the picture: with --debug every change writes "<cell label> -> <value>"
# to p41-debug-events.log, and each row below names the line it must produce. The start date is
# 2025-08-24 09:46:40 (P41RootView.start, local time on this Mac).
#
# origin=frame, window 1202 x 799 points, capture scale 1 (p41-macos-final-20261020-221137.png).
#
# P41:驅動以 SwiftCrossUI view 畫的選擇器(滾輪、列)與 AppKit 自己的時鐘。以 binding 判定:--debug 下每次變更
# 在 p41-debug-events.log 寫一行「<格位標題> -> <值>」,下面每一列都寫明它必須產生的那一行。
